Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; Remainder for Windows -- the typeface substitution. OPT-IN, and HKLM: this is the one thing in
; the kit that needs the elevation the directory is named for. PLATFORM.md records it as out of
; reach per-user -- "Segoe UI Variable in system chrome (needs HKLM FontSubstitutes)" -- which
; under CONTRIBUTING sec. 1 makes it a residue that elevation removes rather than one to tolerate.
;
; DO NOT MERGE THIS UNTIL MONTSERRAT IS INSTALLED. A substitution pointing at a face that is not
; on the machine makes Windows fall back, and the fallback is not a face anybody chose. The kit
; ships no fonts (CONTRIBUTING sec. 12): get Montserrat from the repository its own licence names,
; github.com/JulietaUla/Montserrat, and install the faces before merging this.
;
; AUTHORITY.md sec. 5 declares Montserrat for UI and Hack for mono, and records that the cuts are
; MEDIUM and EXTRABOLD rather than Regular and Bold -- Regular reads thin at 16px, and weight is
; safe in one direction only: every contrast floor in the kit gets easier as rendered weight goes
; up. Windows picks the cut by name from the installed family, so install the Medium and ExtraBold
; faces and the substitution lands on them.
;
; This file is the whole substitution and it is separately reversible: delete these values and
; Windows goes back to Segoe UI. install.cmd only merges it when asked with --fonts.
;
; ASCII, CRLF, no BOM -- see remainder.theme's header for why.

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Microsoft\Windows NT\CurrentVersion\FontSubstitutes]
"Segoe UI"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Light"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Semibold"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Semilight"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Black"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Historic"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Variable"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Variable Display"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Variable Small"="Montserrat"
"Segoe UI Variable Text"="Montserrat"
